---
description: Never add Cursor or AI co-author attribution to git commits or PRs
alwaysApply: true
---

# No Cursor commit attribution

When creating commits or pull requests:

- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Co-authored-by: cursoragent`, `Made-with: Cursor`, or any similar AI/tool attribution trailer.
- Do **not** pass `--trailer` for Cursor/agent attribution.
- Commit messages must contain only the subject/body describing the change.
- If a Cursor environment still injects attribution, strip it before finishing (amend only when amend rules allow; otherwise create a clean replacement commit).

Also remind the user they can turn off IDE attribution at **Cursor Settings → Git & PRs → Attribution** (or **Agent → Attribution** on older versions).
